From 6a86df644f9428f1af8e632247c048b0cdfe8d4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Szewczyk <a.szewczyk@cthings.co>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 13:45:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boards: ct: ctcc: add nRF9151 target and backport DK/dongle
 improvements

The ctcc Connectivity Card board only shipped nRF52840 and nRF9161
targets and had drifted from the upstream nRF52840 Dongle and nRF91 DK
reference boards. Add the missing nRF9151 target and pull in the
relevant reference-board improvements.

- Add ctcc/nrf9151 and ctcc/nrf9151/ns targets (dts, common dtsi,
  pinctrl, defconfigs, yaml), modeled on the nRF9161 target and wired
  into board.yml, Kconfig.ctcc, Kconfig.defconfig and board.cmake.
- nrf91: fix the non-secure application SRAM. Point zephyr,sram at
  sram0_ns_app (128 KB) instead of sram0_ns, whose 168 KB span overlaps
  the 40 KB modem-library IPC region (sram0_ns_modem) and corrupts the
  modem shared memory at runtime. Applied to nRF9161 and nRF9151 NS.
- nrf52840: adopt the zephyr,mapped-partition idiom and enable the second
  GPIO port (&gpio1), matching the nRF52840 Dongle. Reset-as-GPIO (mPCIe/M.2
  PERST#) is left to a per-build overlay rather than baked into the board.
  nfct-pins-as-gpios is deliberately NOT taken from the Dongle: nothing on this
  card uses P0.09/P0.10, and the property costs a UICR write plus a reset on the
  first boot of every card (the MDK applies it from SystemInit) and permanently
  gives up NFC on the part. Add it in an overlay if a firmware ever needs those
  two pins as GPIOs.
- Add the J-Link runner to all targets.
- Size the nRF52840 MCUboot slots for swap-using-move: image-0 and image-1
  are equal (0x75000 each). boot_slots_compatible() in swap_move.c requires
  the primary to equal the secondary (or be at most one sector larger) and
  rejects any other ratio at runtime with "not a compatible amount of
  sectors"; the previous 0x76000/0x74000 (primary +2 sectors) layout would
  refuse every DFU swap. The nRF91 targets keep the Nordic equal-slot layout.
- Fix the external flash JEDEC ID on both nRF91 targets: the MX25R6435FM2IL0
  fitted on the card answers RDID with c2 28 17 (Macronix, MX25R type 0x28,
  64 Mbit), not c2 25 38. With the default SPI_NOR_SFDP_MINIMAL the driver
  compares the read ID against this property and refuses to bind on a mismatch
  (spi_nor.c, -EINVAL), so the external flash was unusable. Every other Zephyr
  board carrying this part uses c2 28 17, and the driver's own MX25R type
  constant is 0x28.
- Enable the on-board external flash (MX25R6435FM2IL0, 64 Mbit on spi3) on both
  nRF91 targets. The card is fitted with it, so the board should present it as
  available; leaving it disabled meant every application had to enable it itself,
  and the Serial Modem silently lost access to it. Note this is not the nRF9151
  DK's part (a gd25wb256), and no "nordic,pm-ext-flash" chosen entry is added
  here: that would hand the flash to Partition Manager for full modem FOTA and
  move the flash layout.
- doc: document the nRF9151 target.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Adam Szewczyk <a.szewczyk@cthings.co>
