 Applications for ``ctcc`` boards can be
 built in the usual way (see :ref:`build_an_application` for more details).
 
+.. note::
+
+   Resetting the card over the mPCIe/M.2 ``PERST#`` line needs ``gpio-as-nreset`` in
+   UICR, and the board devicetree deliberately does not set it: the property is a
+   one-way UICR write plus a reset on the first boot, so it belongs to a deliberate
+   build rather than to every sample someone compiles for this board. A deliberate
+   product build applies an overlay that sets the property for every image it makes,
+   including the bootloader. A sample built straight from this SDK - any of the ones
+   below - therefore has no PERST reset. Add one with an overlay containing::
+
+      &uicr {
+              gpio-as-nreset;
+      };
+
+   passed as ``-DEXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE=<file>``, plus
+   ``-Dmcuboot_EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE=<file>`` when MCUboot is in the build - a card
+   that has only ever run the loader would otherwise have no PERST reset until an
+   application boots once.
+
